      {
        "@type": "Review",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Person",
          "name": "Allyson"
        },
        "datePublished": "2026-07-24",
        "name": "Used to be great. Not so much now.",
        "reviewBody": "I have six of these shelves from years ago and I love them. I recently bought several more and the hardware has really been downgraded. Very disappointing. First, there are no wall screws with this product. The wall screws that came with the older version were excellent. But the biggest issue I have with this product is the bracket itself. This newer version has a shorter bracket and significantly fewer holes to work with for securing it to the wall. Because of the shorter bracket and limited holes, you'll be lucky to catch two studs in the wall. A shelf this size should be able to attach to two studs. While the shelf does span across two studs in my wall, none of the holes are in the proper place for me to access them. I can't slide the shelf over in my case, so I'm left with using anchors exclusively. If you aren't going to include wall hardware, at least provide enough access points in the bracket so that I can safely hang this with my own.",
        "reviewRating": {
          "@type": "Rating",
          "ratingValue": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Review",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Person",
          "name": "Angela"
        },
        "datePublished": "2026-07-20",
        "name": "Beautiful!!",
        "reviewBody": "Love these floating shelves. I hung 2 of the 43\" oak and they are stunning. They look so much more expensive once they are up and styled.",
        "reviewRating": {
          "@type": "Rating",
          "ratingValue": 5
        }
      },
